    "items": [
      {
        "id": "a-year-out",
        "title": "A year out: what to decide first",
        "date": "2026-10-02",
        "intro": "Three things fix everything else. Choose them in this order.",
        "body": [
          "The date, the number and the room decide almost every other choice. Fix the date first if it matters to you; the number next, because it rules out most rooms; then the room.",
          "Flowers, tableware and the menu follow from those three. We start design work once they are settled."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "choosing-a-room",
        "title": "Choosing a room",
        "date": "2026-09-11",
        "intro": "Seated, standing and the space between tables.",
        "body": [
          "A room's capacity is the venue's to give, and it changes with the layout: long tables seat more than rounds, standing takes more again.",
          "Ask the venue for its plan with measurements. We draw your layout on it before you sign."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "candles",
        "title": "Candles, and the rules",
        "date": "2026-08-20",
        "intro": "Every venue has its own.",
        "body": [
          "Many rooms allow only enclosed flames, some none at all. We ask the venue in writing before we design around candlelight."
        ]
      }
    ]
